<header class="ref-head yr-head"><p class="cty-kicker">Year by year · <a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a></p><h1 class="research-title">476 CE</h1><p class="ref-lede">476 CE in world history: 4 events, 1 birth, 1 death, 1 state founded and 1 that came to an end. 168 recorded states existed that year.</p></header>
<nav class="ref-letters yr-near" aria-label="Nearby years"><a href="/years/455">455 CE</a><a href="/years/461">461 CE</a><a href="/years/474">474 CE</a><a href="/years/475">475 CE</a><a href="/years/476" aria-current="page">476 CE</a><a href="/years/484">484 CE</a><a href="/years/493">493 CE</a><a href="/years/499">499 CE</a><a href="/years/502">502 CE</a></nav>
<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/august-23">23 August</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Odoacer is proclaimed king by the foederati in Italy</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">After <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/orestes-roman-general">Orestes</a> refused the Germanic foederati land in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, they and much of the Italic Roman army proclaimed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odoacer">Odoacer</a> king. He then deposed the young emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romulus">Romulus</a>, a takeover traditionally seen as the end of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-roman-empire">Western Roman Empire</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odoacer">Odoacer</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/romulus-augustulus" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/romulus-augustulus.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/september-4">4 September</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Odoacer deposes Romulus Augustulus, the last Western emperor</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Germanic commander <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odoacer">Odoacer</a> deposed the boy emperor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romulus-augustulus">Romulus Augustulus</a> and sent the imperial regalia to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constantinople">Constantinople</a>. The date is conventionally taken as the end of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-roman-empire">Western Roman Empire</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/roman-empire">Roman Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-roman-empire">Western Roman Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romulus-augustulus">Romulus Augustulus</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/odoacer">Odoacer</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">Event</p><h3 class="tih-event-title"><a href="/encyclopedia/fall-of-the-western-roman-empire">Fall of the Western Roman Empire</a></h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The fall of the Western Roman Empire is conventionally dated to 476 CE, when the Germanic commander Odoacer deposed the last western emperor, Romulus Augustulus.</p></div></li></ol></section>
